load("@rules_julia//julia/pkg:defs.bzl", "julia_pkg_resolve_test") julia_pkg_resolve_test(name, resolver) A test rule that verifies the manifests managed by julia_pkg_resolve are up to date. Every manifest is checked under a Julia toolchain of the version it is declared for, by comparing the manifest's recorded project_hash with the hash of the current Project.toml. Pkg's hash algorithm differs between Julia minor versions, which is why the resolver's declaration drives which Julia runs each check. When the resolver also tracks a Manifest.bazel.json, that file is checked against the manifest as well. The test will fail if: A manifest is out of date with respect to Project.toml A manifest was resolved with a different Julia minor version than declared A package is missing from Manifest.bazel.json Versions or UUIDs don't match between the manifest and Manifest.bazel.json The git-tree-sha1 is not in the package URL Integrity values are missing Example: julia_pkg_resolve( name = "pkg_update", project_toml = "Project.toml", manifests = {"Manifest.toml": "1.12"},
) julia_pkg_resolve_test( name = "pkg_sync_test", resolver = ":pkg_update",
) Then run: bazel test //:pkg_sync_test If the files are out of sync the test fails with details on what needs to be regenerated. ATTRIBUTES Name Description Type Mandatory Default name A unique name for this target. Name required resolver The julia_pkg_resolve target whose manifests are checked. Label required

